---
title: Lamb ragu
servings: 8
tags: [italian, lamb, braise, weekend]
cuisine: italian
time: 4 hours 15 minutes
source: Lamb Ragu by Billy Parisi, https://www.billyparisi.com/lamb-ragu
nutrition:
  calories: 228 kcal
  fat: 8 g
  saturated fat: 3 g
  carbohydrates: 16 g
  sugar: 8 g
  protein: 19 g
  fiber: 3 g
  sodium: 452 mg
  serving size: 1 serving
---

Render the @pancetta{4%oz}(diced) in a #rondeau{} over low to medium heat until
crisp. Lift it out and keep it aside.

Cut the @lamb leg{1}(boneless) into pieces of about 8 oz, along with the
@?lamb shank{1} if using. Dry them well and season with @salt{} and
@black pepper{}.

Brown the lamb in the fat over medium heat, fat side first, ~{3-4%minutes} a
side. Set aside.

Add the @onion{1}(large, diced) with a pinch of salt. Cook
~{5%minutes} until it starts to colour, then turn the heat to low and cook
~{10%minutes} more, stirring now and then.

Add the @carrots{3}(peeled, finely diced), @celery{3%stalks}(finely diced) and
@garlic{6%cloves}(smashed). Cover and sweat on low ~{10-12%minutes}.

Pour in the @red wine{3/4%cup} and boil over medium heat ~{5-7%minutes} to
reduce. Stir in the @tomato paste{2%tbsp} and cook ~{2-3%minutes} until it
darkens to rust.

Add the @tomato puree{28%oz}, @beef stock{4%cup}, @parsley{3-4%sprigs},
@thyme{3-4%sprigs}, @rosemary{1%sprig}, @bay leaves{2} and the
@Parmigiano Reggiano rind{1}. Season and stir.

Return the lamb, cover, and cook on low heat or in a 325°F oven, middle rack,
~{2.5-3%hours}, until the lamb is fork-tender.

Fish out the herb stems, rind and any bones. Pull the lamb apart in the sauce
with two forks.

Stir in @lemon juice{1-1.5%tbsp}(from half a lemon). Serve over pasta with
the crisp pancetta and chopped @parsley{} on top.
